  "slug": "pangenome-graphs-bd3e",
  "summary": "Graph-aware and k-mer representations are beginning to replace variant calls and linear references in haplotype, germline and ancestry analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is moving haplotype and ancestry inference off the linear reference and onto graph or k-mer representations of many genomes. GRASER phases graph-aligned short reads directly against individual haplotype paths using unique graph edges, avoiding linear-reference bias. A population-scale pangenome analysis of 232 individuals with gAIRR Suite v2 identifies 531 novel TR germline alleles and reports 99.985% recall. KORUS instead infers ancestry from k-mer Bloom filter representations without variant calls, supporting classification, admixture fractions and population structure. The imprinting study models direct, maternal, paternal and parent-of-origin effects on 850k blood methylation probes in 2,438 trios; it is methylation-based rather than graph-based. The shared element across the set is departure from variant-call or linear-reference inputs, and the methylome study is included as a distinct application that separates imprinting from indirect parental effects.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
